1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,116
You press send max.

2
00:00:02,116 --> 00:00:05,747
But what happens when the fee comes from that same balance?

3
00:00:07,002 --> 00:00:11,193
On Arc, the money and the gas are the same USDC.

4
00:00:11,193 --> 00:00:14,028
Every transaction needs a network fee,

5
00:00:14,028 --> 00:00:16,788
paid from the balance you're sending.

6
00:00:16,788 --> 00:00:21,252
Try to send every cent, and nothing is left to pay for it.

7
00:00:22,528 --> 00:00:25,612
LastDollar shows what you can actually send,

8
00:00:25,612 --> 00:00:27,154
what the fee may cost,

9
00:00:27,154 --> 00:00:30,379
and what remains, before you approve anything.

10
00:00:31,646 --> 00:00:36,387
This is the live app on Arc mainnet, with real USDC.

11
00:00:36,387 --> 00:00:38,490
I am connected with MetaMask,

12
00:00:38,490 --> 00:00:42,116
using a small wallet that holds about three cents.

13
00:00:42,116 --> 00:00:45,018
I will send its maximum to my other wallet.

14
00:00:46,284 --> 00:00:49,745
I choose Send maximum, and native USDC.

15
00:00:49,745 --> 00:00:53,183
LastDollar estimates the real transaction,

16
00:00:53,183 --> 00:00:58,094
sets aside a maximum fee budget, and offers everything else.

17
00:00:58,094 --> 00:01:01,561
The estimated fee is what it will probably cost.

18
00:01:01,561 --> 00:01:04,061
The budget is the most it can cost.

19
00:01:05,314 --> 00:01:09,033
Because the real fee is usually below the budget,

20
00:01:09,033 --> 00:01:11,082
a tiny amount stays behind.

21
00:01:11,082 --> 00:01:13,396
LastDollar says so up front,

22
00:01:13,396 --> 00:01:16,454
instead of promising an empty wallet.

23
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:19,694
Before anything is signed,

24
00:01:19,694 --> 00:01:22,655
I confirm the recipient and the amount.

25
00:01:22,655 --> 00:01:28,012
When I continue, LastDollar rechecks my balance, nonce and fees.

26
00:01:28,012 --> 00:01:31,806
If anything changed, it would ask me to review again.

27
00:01:33,078 --> 00:01:35,959
Then I approve the payment in MetaMask.

28
00:01:37,228 --> 00:01:38,323
Confirmed.

29
00:01:38,323 --> 00:01:41,359
LastDollar reads the receipt from the chain.

30
00:01:41,359 --> 00:01:44,676
The recipient got exactly the reviewed amount,

31
00:01:44,676 --> 00:01:46,046
and the actual fee,

32
00:01:46,046 --> 00:01:50,228
less than a twentieth of a cent, stayed inside the budget.

33
00:01:50,228 --> 00:01:54,216
What is left in the wallet is the unused part of that budget.

34
00:01:55,490 --> 00:01:58,103
Anyone can check it on the Arc explorer.

35
00:01:58,103 --> 00:02:01,228
The proof page lists the mainnet payments,

36
00:02:01,228 --> 00:02:05,841
and re-verifies each one live from the chain, in your browser.

37
00:02:07,104 --> 00:02:09,248
LastDollar is open source,

38
00:02:09,248 --> 00:02:14,524
with a TypeScript SDK so other Arc apps can use the same checks.

39
00:02:14,524 --> 00:02:17,426
Try it at lastdollar dot vercel dot app.
